What follows for apps/web when the settled design is implemented there:

1. The style sheet will be about the size of the file that the real app ships today, not larger. Counted from the lab files of the six pages, with the entry of the real app (tailwindcss + ui.css): 400,242 B raw, 53,551 gzip, 37,675 brotli with the whole new primitives folder; 316,888 B raw, 44,554 gzip, 32,182 brotli when the five recipes that the design does not reach are not scanned. Today: 464,666 B built (32,868 brotli), of which 114,948 B are duplicate rules; 332,367 B after the duplicate is fixed. This is an estimate: the real pages will have other class names than the lab files.

2. The file size will not make the real app slow in production. The parse is about 12 ms with the CPU slowed 4 times, the sheet is one cached request of 32 to 38 KB brotli, and the real app has 1 document, not 11.

3. The cost that does go to the real app is the style work for each element. It grows with the count of elements, not with the file. The history page of the lab has 1,116 elements and 354,513 characters of HTML (18,153 B gzip), and style recalculation was 749 ms with the CPU slowed 4 times even with the smallest possible sheet. So in the real app, limit the rows that a list renders (paging or a window), and measure the long lists first.

4. Three changes in apps/web keep its development fast, each one small:

```css
/* apps/web/src/review.css or the one entry that stays */
@import "tailwindcss" source("./");
@import "./components/ariakit/styles/ui.css";
@source not "./components/ariakit/styles/tabs.ts";
@source not "./components/ariakit/styles/table.ts";
@source not "./components/ariakit/styles/choice.ts";
```

- Compile the sheet one time (audit finding FE-09: styles.css imports review.css, and two TSX files import review.css again). The lab shows the result: 1 copy in development and 0 duplicate rules in the build, against 2 and 4 copies and 581 duplicate rules.
- An explicit source, so that a write to CHANGELOG.md, migrations, or tooling does not reload the page.
- No scan of the recipes that the app does not use (83,354 B for the design: tabs.ts, choice.ts, table.ts, checkbox.ts, radio.ts). Do not remove a `@source not` line before a page uses that primitive.

5. For Ariakit: the three things that would lower the cost for every app are (a) recipes whose unused variants do not reach the sheet (one Button is 118,820 B today), (b) ak-* value utilities that set only an input variable, with the formula in one class (72,313 B of repeated blocks in this sheet, `@utility ak-ink-*` at src/output.css line 816 is the clearest case), (c) fewer classes for each element (19 for a Text, 29 for a control slot, 65 for a glider).
